# Kecktech.net Project Rules

## Project Purpose

Senior citizen IT support business: remote support, bundled services, and HaaS (Hardware as a Service) with concierge-level support. All apps are self-hosted on this VM; all containers run here. Build and configure everything in the test environment first; do not configure Cloudflare until all applications are configured and ready to deploy (see Phase 8 in PROJECT_PLAN.md).

## Stack (Do Not Substitute Without Explicit Approval)

| Function | Tool | Notes |
|----------|------|--------|
| ERP/Admin | ERPNext | CRM, HaaS, accounting, HR, dispatch |
| Help Desk | FreeScout | Email-based tickets; helpdesk.kecktech.net |
| Billing/Invoicing | ERPNext | All invoicing, recurring billing, HaaS, client payments (no Invoice Ninja) |
| Remote Access | RustDesk | Senior screen-sharing bridge |
| Secrets/Client Profiles | Vaultwarden | WiFi passwords, printer models, access keys |
| Workflow/SMS | n8n | Trigger SMS (e.g. Twilio) on high-priority tickets |
| Public Website | WordPress | Marketing, "About the Founder," lead capture; Astra theme + Spectra/Gutenberg blocks (not Elementor) |
| Knowledge Base | WikiJS | Senior-friendly how-tos; support video; high-contrast theme; help.kecktech.net |
| SSO | Authelia + LLDAP | Single login for all internal apps (dashboard, ERPNext, FreeScout, n8n, Vaultwarden) |
| RMM | Tactical RMM | Patching, alerts, remote shells |
| Analytics | Umami | Privacy-first, no PII |
| Payments | Stripe | Via ERPNext; ACH/CC |
| Network access | Tailscale | VM joined to workspace; staff/admin access to internal apps; SSH locked to Tailscale interface |
| Mail | Mailcow | Self-hosted; support@kecktech.net and admin@kecktech.net; own compose stack at Dashboard/mailcow/ |

## Best Practices

- **Containers**: All services run in Docker. Prefer one `docker-compose.yml` (or grouped compose files) for the stack; document any split.
- **Test environment**: Use Traefik as the reverse proxy with the same hostnames as production. Point all subdomains to the VM's **Tailscale IP** via `/etc/hosts` on every test machine — this makes the stack reachable from anywhere on the Tailscale network without port forwarding.
- **Production (when ready)**: Cloudflare Tunnel for **public-facing apps only** (`kecktech.net`, `help.kecktech.net`, `helpdesk.kecktech.net`). All internal/staff apps remain accessible only over Tailscale — never exposed publicly. Zero open inbound ports. Do not configure Cloudflare until the full stack is built and verified in test (Phase 8).
- **App-to-app communication**: Prefer webhooks and REST APIs. Document every integration (e.g. FreeScout → n8n → Twilio, ERPNext ↔ Stripe, ticket creation from CRM). Use shared env vars or a small config service for URLs/secrets; never hardcode.
- **Secrets**: Store in Vaultwarden or env files (not in repo). Reference in compose as env vars or Docker secrets.
- **Backups**: Assume Proxmox snapshots + app-level backups (DB dumps, config exports) to NAS or S3. Document restore steps.
- **Accessibility**: Knowledge base and client-facing content must support high-contrast (e.g. black/white/yellow) and consider text-to-speech for seniors.

## Integration Points to Maintain

1. **Lead → Ticket**: CRM/ERPNext or WordPress form creates or links to FreeScout ticket.
2. **Ticket → Dispatch**: High-priority FreeScout ticket triggers n8n → SMS (Twilio) to Florida contact.
3. **Billing**: All invoicing and HaaS in ERPNext; Stripe for collection.
4. **RMM + Help Desk**: Tactical RMM alerts can create or link to FreeScout tickets where applicable.
5. **Single dashboard**: Custom app (Next.js or static) at dashboard.kecktech.net with tiles and health checks; SSO (Authelia) for single login to all internal apps.

## Conventions

- **Config as code**: Compose files, Cloudflare config, and app configs (where possible) live in version control.
- **Document in PROJECT_PLAN.md**: Any new phase or step gets a clear entry; update the plan when the stack or flow changes.
- **No mock data** in production paths unless explicitly requested.
- **Windows**: Development may be on Windows; production is Linux (Ubuntu VM). Use cross-platform commands or document OS-specific steps.
- **Container locations**: All app stacks live under the project. Main stack: `Dashboard/docker/` (docker-compose.yml). ERPNext: `Dashboard/erpnext/frappe_docker/`. Run `./startup-all` from Dashboard to start the main stack.
